  "behavior": [
    "Per-origin EVM grant revisions bind queued requests to id, allowed status, account and selected network. Revocation/removal/change followed by restoration invalidates an old request; unrelated-origin or non-authority changes do not. Missing legacy revisions fail approval validation.",
    "Admission waits for initial loading then captures current state. Approval reads an isolated current snapshot synchronously at each final key-export, transaction-broadcast or signature-release boundary; storage reads cannot yield between the authority check and local submission.",
    "Authorization intent becomes authoritative in memory immediately. Stored snapshots are separate from caller/cache objects; older write completion and late initial reads cannot restore old authority. Reads and subscription publications return detached values.",
    "Existing extension/web stores serialize persistence. An outer intent is enqueued before initial-load waiters run, preserving ordering when a waiter publishes a newer intent. No second persistence queue is introduced.",
    "EVM revocation, Solana/Iroha disconnect, origin removal and account-scope changes atomically transform the latest cache after loading rather than republishing a stale whole map. Network activation additionally requires its captured origin revision to remain unchanged.",
    "Cross-protocol approval preserves untouched scopes from the current allowed record; it rejects and consumes an approval whose origin was removed/replaced/globally changed. Explicit reauthorization from a denied record grants only the approved protocol and does not revive retained EVM/Substrate/Iroha scopes. Current selected network is retained."
  ],
